{"id": "g3_min_sixfold_shifted_quotient", "signature": "solve(readings)", "statement": "Given a list of integers `readings`, consider the entries divisible by 6 (zero counts, and so do negative entries such as -6 and -12). For each such entry compute entry // 6 + 1, where // is Python floor division (exact here, since the entry is divisible by 6), and return the SMALLEST of these results. If no entry is divisible by 6, including for an empty list, return None.", "tests": [{"args": [[]], "expected": null}, {"args": [[1, 5, 7]], "expected": null}, {"args": [[0]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[-6, 12, 18]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[6, 6, -12, 30]], "expected": -1}, {"args": [[-18]], "expected": -2}, {"args": [[7, 11, 13]], "expected": null}, {"args": [[24, 0, -24, 36]], "expected": -3}, {"args": [[-30, -6]], "expected": -4}, {"args": [[5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[-4, -36, -48, 4, 53, 18]], "expected": -7}, {"args": [[36, 55, -24, 50]], "expected": -3}, {"args": [[38, 0, -15, 26, 0, 44, 58, -14, -57, 7, -3]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[6, -13, -47, 30, 23, -13]], "expected": 2}, {"args": [[-14, -51, -56]], "expected": null}, {"args": [[-14, -24, -2, -10, -1, 29, 11, 1, 28, -4]], "expected": -3}, {"args": [[-9, -8, 32, -42, -30, 14, -34, 17, 12, -5]], "expected": -6}], "facts": [["arg", "readings", "int_list"], ["iterate", "readings"], ["remainder", "6", "0"], ["floordiv", "6"], ["add", "1"], ["aggregate", "min"], ["if_empty", "none"], ["size", "readings", "tiny"]], "deps": {"schema": ["seq_fold"], "uses": [], "solution_sha256": "eb73bff5e70f49f7b4a01632e94a0fb317c39bb1ca37ca5a7459d07949923eea", "reference_sha256": "60a8f5e0e25a0d23327f39d375000f61f7f3b9b2a3f57a5a51c7520045451850"}}